    {
      "id": "d27r35v1u",
      "node_id": "node-user-lifestyle-input-(card-recommendation)-d9e1d588",
      "version_tag": "v1",
      "title": "User Lifestyle Input (Card Recommendation)",
      "description": {
        "text": {
          "text": {
            "text": {
              "text": {
                "text": {
                  "text": {
                    "text": {
                      "text": "Normalizes user lifestyle preferences and existing card data into a pipe‑delimited string for card ranking.\n\nThis node maps manual lifestyle and preference inputs from a second screen into a standardized pipe‑delimited string used by the credit card ranking engine. It accepts eight inputs: skip optimization flag, existing cards list, first card indicator, annual domestic/international flights, vehicle usage, reward preference, and fee tolerance. The node first checks if optimization should be skipped — if true, it returns an empty string. It then applies a critical logic override: if the user holds no existing cards (i.e., “None”), the first card indicator is forcibly set to “None” to prevent contradictory input. After cleaning the values, it builds a string following the format ExistingCards: <value> | FirstCard: <value> | DomesticFlights: <value> | InternationalFlights: <value> | DrivesVehicle: <value> | RewardPref: <value> | FeeTolerance: <value>. This output enables downstream recommendation nodes to personalize card suggestions based on travel habits, fuel usage, reward preferences, and fee sensitivity, while respecting the user’s existing credit card portfolio.",
                      "lineHeight": 14,
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
                    },
                    "lineHeight": 14,
                    "fontSize": 11,
                    "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
                  },
                  "lineHeight": 14,
                  "fontSize": 11,
                  "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
                },
                "lineHeight": 14,
                "fontSize": 11,
                "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
              },
              "lineHeight": 14,
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
            },
            "lineHeight": 14,
            "fontSize": 11,
            "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
          },
          "lineHeight": 14,
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
        },
        "lineHeight": 14,
        "fontSize": 11,
        "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "node_id": "node-user-lifestyle-input-(card-recommendation)-d9e1d588",
        "name": "User Lifestyle Input (Card Recommendation)",
        "description": "Normalizes user lifestyle preferences and existing card data into a pipe‑delimited string for card ranking.\n\nThis node maps manual lifestyle and preference inputs from a second screen into a standardized pipe‑delimited string used by the credit card ranking engine. It accepts eight inputs: skip optimization flag, existing cards list, first card indicator, annual domestic/international flights, vehicle usage, reward preference, and fee tolerance. The node first checks if optimization should be skipped — if true, it returns an empty string. It then applies a critical logic override: if the user holds no existing cards (i.e., “None”), the first card indicator is forcibly set to “None” to prevent contradictory input. After cleaning the values, it builds a string following the format ExistingCards: <value> | FirstCard: <value> | DomesticFlights: <value> | InternationalFlights: <value> | DrivesVehicle: <value> | RewardPref: <value> | FeeTolerance: <value>. This output enables downstream recommendation nodes to personalize card suggestions based on travel habits, fuel usage, reward preferences, and fee sensitivity, while respecting the user’s existing credit card portfolio.",
